                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              A complete Boolean algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              is completely distributive iff it is atomic (a
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CABA"} CABA
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
              as a Boolean algebra.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              For a complete atomic Boolean algebra
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi atoms
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to P(atoms(B))
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in B
              to the set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atoms"} atoms
              below it, is an isomorphism. Such
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+sets"} power sets
              are products of copies of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2} = \{0 \leq 1\}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
              of completely distributive lattices are completely distributive.
            %p
              In the other direction, suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              is completely distributive. Take
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 2
                      %mo :
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = \pi_2: \mathbf{2} \times B \to B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha: \mathbf{2} \times B \to B
              by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha(0, b) \coloneqq \neg b
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha(1, b) \coloneqq b
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              correspond to functions
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g: B \to \mathbf{2}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∨
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo :
                        %mi B
                        %mo →
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 2
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi B
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 = \bigwedge_{b \in B} (b \vee \neg b) = \bigvee_{g: B \to \mathbf{2}} \bigwedge_{b \in B} \alpha(g(b), b).
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a(g)
              as abbreviation for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                        %mrow
                          %mi b
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi B
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigwedge_{b \in B} \alpha(g(b), b)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∧
                    %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∧
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo :
                        %mi B
                        %mo →
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 2
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo :
                        %mi B
                        %mo →
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 2
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b = b \wedge 1 = b \wedge \bigvee_{g: B \to \mathbf{2}} a(g) = \bigvee_{g: B \to \mathbf{2}} b \wedge a(g)
            %p
              so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≠
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \wedge a(g) \neq 0
              for some
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              if
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ≠
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \neq 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≠
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \wedge a(g) \neq 0
              implies
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(b) = 1
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  Whenever
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \leq a(g)
                  with
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi b
                          %mo ≠
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \neq 0
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi α
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi α
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi b
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a(g) \leq \alpha(g(b), b) = \alpha(1, b) = b
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a(g)
                  is an atom whenever
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ≠
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a(g) \neq 0
              %li
                %p
                  Provided that
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi b
                          %mo ∧
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ≠
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \wedge a(g) \neq 0
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a(g)
                  is an atom below
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi b
                          %mo ∧
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi b
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \wedge a(g) \leq b
            %p
              The last point shows every element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              has an atom
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a(g)
              below it, so that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              is atomic, as was to be shown.
          %h3#constructive_complete_distributivity Constructive complete distributivity
          %p
            A complete lattice
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is called
            %strong constructively completely distributive
            (CCD) if the join-assigning morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D A \to A
            has a left adjoint, with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D A
            the poset of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/downsets"} downsets
          %p
            %em
              Constructive complete distributivity is equivalent to complete distributivity if and only if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              holds
            (
            %a{:href => "#WoodFawcett"}> Wood&amp;Fawcett (1990)
            ).
          %p
            Constructively completely distributive lattices are an example of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+algebras"} continuous algebras
            for a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax-idempotent+2-monad"} lax-idempotent 2-monad
          %h3#remark Remark
          %p
            Completely distributive lattices correspond to tight
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+connections"} Galois connections
            (Raney 1953). This generalizes to a correspondence between totally distributive toposes and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+geometric+morphism"} essential localizations
            (Lucyshyn-Wright 2011).
          %p
            CCD lattices are precisely the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nuclear+objects"} nuclear objects
            in the category of complete lattices.
          %p
            The (bi-) category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℭℭ𝔇
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{CCD}
            with CCD lattices and sup-preserving maps is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karoubi+envelope"} idempotent splitting
            of the (bi-) category of relations
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℜ𝔢𝔩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{Rel}
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"}> domain
              \-theoretical
            approaches to the semantics of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+logic"} linear logic
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+lattice"} continuous lattice
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/totally+distributive+category"} totally distributive category
          %h2#links Links
          %ul
            %li
              wikipedia-entry:
              %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Completely_distributive_lattice"} completely distributive lattice
          %h2#references References
          %ul#Caramello11
